-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 30.12.2009 — עובדי ההוראה בשירות המדינה ותיקון חוק
-- הגמלאות: the State and הסתדרות המורים settle, after the Pensions Law was
-- amended in 2002, how the change is carried out for the teaching employees
-- in the State's service. Registered on 15.3.2010 (no. 18/2010). General
-- (chapter א'); definitions — teaching employee, permanent, existing and
-- new, the determining day (31.8.2002), the Pensions Law, the budgetary
-- track, the provident-fund law, an accrual fund and an expense
-- reimbursement (ב'); whom it covers (ג'); the permanent teaching employee,
-- who stays on the budgetary pension and has accrual contributions from
-- 1.1.2009 on his other components (ד'); the existing and the new one,
-- insured in an accrual fund on a base of (א) and (ב) together (ה'); the
-- rates, 13.5% and 13.724% with 5.5% from the employee (ו'); severance, 72%
-- and 28% (ז'); money back to the State (ח'); choosing the fund (ט');
-- carrying it out, equal terms, earlier terms, disputes, commencement on
-- 1.1.2009, exhaustion and registration (י'–ט"ז).
--
-- It follows the public sector's transition agreement of 3.3.1999
-- (l4/agreements/framework/1999-03-03_framework-agreement_public-sector_pension-transition.l4,
-- imported), which leaves the teaching scale out (its chapter ג' §1(ב)):
-- where its words are that agreement's, the rule is imported under this
-- agreement's name. Its contributions on components take the place of the
-- provident-fund agreement of 17.12.98 (הסכם הגמל:
-- l4/agreements/teachers-general/1998-12-17_histadrut-hamorim_provident-fund.l4,
-- imported) where the two would meet, and of §9 of that agreement. It
-- speaks to no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is in no root.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `1998-12-17_histadrut-hamorim_provident-fund`
IMPORT `1999-03-03_framework-agreement_public-sector_pension-transition`
IMPORT severance_pay_law
IMPORT wage_protection_law

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: chapter ח' names a teacher
-- who resigned or was dismissed only as the case in which the fund returns
-- the State's contributions, and chapter ז' an event entitling to severance
-- only as when its 28% is paid; neither gives or asks notice, so they rule
-- nothing the law puts a floor under.

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: a position "up to
-- 100%" is the base of the contributions and of severance, a share of a
-- position; the agreement sets no working hour, day or week.

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — עובדי ההוראה בשירות המדינה: מפנסיה תקציבית לפנסיה צוברת (30.12.2009)`

DECLARE `2009 teachers' pension action` IS ONE OF
    `notify the State of the funds the union chose`
    `support the steps the 2009 pension agreement needs`
    `follow, assist and decide disputes over the 2009 pension agreement`
    `discuss returning the State's share on a component the budgetary pension pays`
    `submit the 2009 pension agreement for registration`

`why the Pensions Law and the other laws it cites are not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שירות המדינה (גמלאות) [נוסח משולב], התש\"ל-1970 (סעיפים 8, 107ב ו־108א); חוק שירות המדינה (מינויים), התשי\"ט-1959; תקנות שירות המדינה (מינויים) (חוזה מיוחד), התש\"ך-1960; חוק הפיקוח על שירותים פיננסיים (קופות גמל), התשס\"ה-2005; חוק הפיקוח על שירותים פיננסיים (ביטוח), התשמ\"א-1981"

`why the other agreements it names are not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "ההסכם הקיבוצי מיום 16.12.02 (הסדר ביניים); ההסכם הקיבוצי בעניין פנסיה תקציבית מיום 31.8.08; מכתב הממונה על השכר מיום 3.3.99"

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The registration stamp (15.3.2010, no. 18/2010); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 The State, by the wages commissioner and the Ministry of Education's director-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 הסתדרות המורים, by its secretary-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

-- ¶3: signed on 30 December 2009, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the 2009 teachers' pension agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 12 2009

-- ¶10–¶15: the recitals. On 6.2.02 the Pensions Law was amended so that it
-- does not apply to one appointed on or after the determining day that
-- applies to him, and new employees are insured from it in an accrual fund;
-- its §108א sends the insurance of components outside the determining
-- salary to a collective agreement the Minister of Finance approves; for
-- the teaching scale the Minister set 31.8.02 as the determining day; an
-- interim agreement was signed on 16.12.02; the parties negotiated and now
-- anchor what they agreed.
@ref akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15
`the 2009 agreement carries out the Pensions Law's amendment for the teaching scale` MEANS TRUE

§§ `פרק א' — כללי`

-- akn:chp_1 The heading of chapter א'.

-- §1: the preamble and annexes are part of it. §2: its headings are for
-- convenience only and do not bear on its reading. §3: the masculine
-- includes the feminine and the plural, and the other way round, unless
-- said otherwise.
@ref akn:chp_1__art_1
`the 2009 pension agreement's preamble and annexes are part of it` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:chp_1__art_2
`the 2009 pension agreement's headings bear on its reading` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:chp_1__art_3
`the 2009 pension agreement's words reach women and men alike` MEANS TRUE

§§ `פרק ב' — הגדרות`

-- akn:chp_2 The heading of chapter ב'.
-- akn:chp_2__art_1 The heading of §1: teaching employee, permanent, existing and new.

-- The determining day (§2) and commencement (chapter י"ד, 1.1.2009).
@ref akn:chp_2__art_2
`the 2009 agreement's determining day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2002

-- §3: the Pensions Law; §5: the provident-fund law; §6: an accrual fund
-- is a provident fund for an annuity as that law defines it. Outside the
-- corpus (above).
-- akn:chp_2__art_3 The Pensions Law, named; outside the corpus.
-- akn:chp_2__art_5 The Provident Funds Law of 2005, named; outside the corpus.
-- akn:chp_2__art_6 An accrual fund, by that law's definition; outside the corpus.

-- §4: the budgetary track is the Pensions Law with what is made under it,
-- and/or the budgetary-pension agreement of 31.8.08 for the teachers who
-- moved to the reform (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:chp_2__art_4 akn:chp_2__art_4/p2
`the budgetary track of the 2009 agreement rests on the Pensions Law and the agreement of 31.8.08` MEANS TRUE

-- The facts of a teaching employee the definitions ask. A paragraph of
-- §107ב of the Pensions Law is a number, 0 where none applies to him.
DECLARE `2009 pension teacher` HAS
    `in the State's service in the teaching scale`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a special or a directors-general contract`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `outside the Appointments Law by its section 2(3), 2(4) or 2(5)`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a workplace outside the Appointments Law, on an accrual pension by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a State employee or an employee as the Pensions Law defines them`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the paragraph of section 107ב of the Pensions Law that applies to him` IS A NUMBER
    `employed continuously from the determining day to the commencement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `insured in an accrual fund on the determining day`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `had finished the probation period on the determining day`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `hired after the determining day`                                     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN low IS A NUMBER, high IS A NUMBER, t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 107ב applies to him by a paragraph from` low `to` high t IF
        t's `the paragraph of section 107ב of the Pensions Law that applies to him` AT LEAST low
    AND t's `the paragraph of section 107ב of the Pensions Law that applies to him` AT MOST high

-- "עובד הוראה": employed in the State's service in the teaching scale,
-- save (1) one on a special contract under regulation 1(3) or a
-- directors-general contract under 1(18), while so employed; (2) one the
-- Appointments Law does not reach by its §2(3), 2(4) or 2(5); (3) one in a
-- workplace the Appointments Law does not reach by its §2(6), insured in an
-- accrual pension under a collective agreement there.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__hc_1
GIVEN t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a teaching employee of 30.12.2009` t IF
        t's `in the State's service in the teaching scale`
    AND NOT t's `on a special or a directors-general contract`
    AND NOT t's `outside the Appointments Law by its section 2(3), 2(4) or 2(5)`
    AND NOT t's `in a workplace outside the Appointments Law, on an accrual pension by agreement`

-- "עובד הוראה קבוע": (1) a "State employee" or "employee" as the Pensions
-- Law defines them; (2) one to whom one of §107ב(1)–(4) of it applies;
-- ¶2: including such a one under the budgetary-pension agreement of 31.8.08.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__hc_2
GIVEN t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a permanent teaching employee as §1 defines one` t IF
        `a teaching employee of 30.12.2009` t
    AND (    t's `a State employee or an employee as the Pensions Law defines them`
         OR  `section 107ב applies to him by a paragraph from` 1 `to` 4 t)

-- "עובד הוראה קיים": employed continuously in the State's service from the
-- determining day to the commencement, both included, who (1) was insured
-- in an accrual fund on the determining day, or (2) had not finished the
-- probation period on it and was not insured in one on it — save one to
-- whom §107ב(1) or 107ב(2) applies.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__hc_3
GIVEN t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing teaching employee as §1 defines one` t IF
        `a teaching employee of 30.12.2009` t
    AND t's `employed continuously from the determining day to the commencement`
    AND (    t's `insured in an accrual fund on the determining day`
         OR  NOT t's `had finished the probation period on the determining day`)
    AND NOT `section 107ב applies to him by a paragraph from` 1 `to` 2 t

-- "עובד הוראה חדש": hired, or to be hired, after the determining day, save
-- one to whom one of §107ב(1)–(4) applies.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__hc_4
GIVEN t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new teaching employee as §1 defines one` t IF
        `a teaching employee of 30.12.2009` t
    AND t's `hired after the determining day`
    AND NOT `section 107ב applies to him by a paragraph from` 1 `to` 4 t

-- F-teachers-pension-2009-a: the permanent definition takes in all of
-- §107ב(1)–(4), and so does the new one's exception; the existing one's
-- exception names only (1) and (2). A teacher insured in an accrual fund on
-- the determining day, employed through to the commencement, to whom
-- §107ב(3) or (4) applies, is both permanent (chapter ד': the budgetary
-- pension, 13.5%) and existing (chapter ה': an accrual fund, 13.724%).
GIVEN `the paragraph of §107ב` IS A NUMBER
      `continuous to the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hired after the determining day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `2009 pension teacher`
DECIDE `a 2009 pension example teacher` `the paragraph of §107ב` `continuous to the commencement` `hired after the determining day` IS
    `2009 pension teacher` WITH
        `in the State's service in the teaching scale`                        IS TRUE
        `on a special or a directors-general contract`                         IS FALSE
        `outside the Appointments Law by its section 2(3), 2(4) or 2(5)`       IS FALSE
        `in a workplace outside the Appointments Law, on an accrual pension by agreement` IS FALSE
        `a State employee or an employee as the Pensions Law defines them`    IS FALSE
        `the paragraph of section 107ב of the Pensions Law that applies to him` IS `the paragraph of §107ב`
        `employed continuously from the determining day to the commencement`  IS `continuous to the commencement`
        `insured in an accrual fund on the determining day`                   IS TRUE
        `had finished the probation period on the determining day`            IS TRUE
        `hired after the determining day`                                     IS `hired after the determining day`

`a teacher of §107ב(3), insured on the determining day` MEANS `a 2009 pension example teacher` 3 TRUE FALSE

`a teacher of §107ב(3) or (4) is both permanent and existing` MEANS
        `a permanent teaching employee as §1 defines one` `a teacher of §107ב(3), insured on the determining day`
    AND `an existing teaching employee as §1 defines one` `a teacher of §107ב(3), insured on the determining day`
#ASSERT `a teacher of §107ב(3) or (4) is both permanent and existing`

-- The reading adopted (convention reading.consistent): §107ב(1)–(4) is one
-- group throughout — the permanent definition takes it in whole and the new
-- one leaves it out whole — so a teacher of any of its paragraphs is
-- permanent, and existing or new only when he is not permanent.
DECLARE `2009 teaching employee's status` IS ONE OF
    `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement`
    `existing, under the 2009 pension agreement`
    `new, under the 2009 pension agreement`
    `none of the 2009 pension agreement's kinds`

GIVEN t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
GIVETH A `2009 teaching employee's status`
DECIDE `the 2009 status of` t IS
    BRANCH IF `a permanent teaching employee as §1 defines one` t THEN `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement`
           IF `an existing teaching employee as §1 defines one` t THEN `existing, under the 2009 pension agreement`
           IF `a new teaching employee as §1 defines one` t THEN `new, under the 2009 pension agreement`
           OTHERWISE `none of the 2009 pension agreement's kinds`

#ASSERT `the 2009 status of` `a teacher of §107ב(3), insured on the determining day` EQUALS `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement`
#ASSERT `the 2009 status of` (`a 2009 pension example teacher` 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `existing, under the 2009 pension agreement`
#ASSERT `the 2009 status of` (`a 2009 pension example teacher` 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `new, under the 2009 pension agreement`

-- §7: an expense reimbursement is every reimbursement of expenses — car
-- costs fixed or variable, compulsory and comprehensive car insurance, the
-- licence fee, travel, subsistence, meals and the like. The kinds of
-- payment the agreement tells apart:
@ref akn:chp_2__art_7
DECLARE `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart` IS ONE OF
    `a component of the budgetary determining salary, of 2009`
    `clothing paid to the budgetary track's retirees, of 2009`
    `recuperation pay or the jubilee grant, of 2009`
    `an expense reimbursement, of 2009`
    `a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit, of 2009`
    `another salary component, of 2009`

§§ `פרק ג' — תחולה`

-- akn:chp_3 The heading of chapter ג'.

-- §1: from the commencement, on every permanent, existing and new teaching
-- employee in the State's service, in the workplaces where a teaching
-- employee could join the budgetary track until the determining day,
-- whether or not he moved to the reform of 10.9.07 or 25.12.08. §2: not in
-- a workplace where, until the determining day and after it, the teaching
-- employees were on an accrual pension by a collective agreement and could
-- not join the budgetary track on its eve, even after tenure.
@ref akn:chp_3__art_1 akn:chp_3__art_2
GIVEN t IS A `2009 pension teacher`
      `could join the budgetary track there until the determining day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2009 pension agreement applies to` t `could join the budgetary track there until the determining day` IF
        NOT `the 2009 status of` t EQUALS `none of the 2009 pension agreement's kinds`
    AND `could join the budgetary track there until the determining day`

#ASSERT NOT `the 2009 pension agreement applies to` `a teacher of §107ב(3), insured on the determining day` FALSE

-- §3(א): at other employers — budgeted or supported bodies as the Budget
-- Foundations Law defines them — in workplaces where on the determining day
-- a teaching employee could join the budgetary track (by the Pensions Law's
-- adoption too), it is carried out if an agreement on the move is reached
-- there and the Minister of Finance approves it, within this agreement's
-- cost. (ב): elsewhere at those employers, only with the wages
-- commissioner's approval, as his letter of 3.3.99 sets, with the changes
-- teaching needs; his signature here approves nothing for them.
@ref akn:chp_3__art_3 akn:chp_3__art_3__para_a akn:chp_3__art_3__para_b
GIVEN `could join the budgetary track there on the determining day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement on the move, approved by the Minister of Finance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wages commissioner approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within this agreement's cost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2009 pension agreement is carried out at a budgeted or supported body` `could join the budgetary track there on the determining day` `an agreement on the move, approved by the Minister of Finance` `the wages commissioner approved it` `within this agreement's cost` IF
    IF `could join the budgetary track there on the determining day`
    THEN `an agreement on the move, approved by the Minister of Finance` AND `within this agreement's cost`
    ELSE `the wages commissioner approved it`

`the wages commissioner's signature approves it for the budgeted and supported bodies` MEANS FALSE

§§ `פרק ד' — עובד הוראה קבוע`

-- akn:chp_4 The heading of chapter ד'.

-- §1: the permanent teaching employees stay on the budgetary track. §2:
-- the "determining salary for the budgetary pension" is the track's
-- determining salary, with recuperation, clothing and the jubilee grant
-- that the track pays its retirees.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_1 akn:chp_4__art_2
`a permanent teaching employee stays on the budgetary track` MEANS TRUE

-- §3: from 1.1.09, contributions and deductions to an accrual fund for
-- the permanent teaching employees, on every component, for a position up
-- to 100%, outside the determining salary for the budgetary pension and not
-- an expense reimbursement, a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit. §4: by
-- the law that applies.
-- §7(ב): the provident-fund contribution of the agreement of 17.12.98 goes
-- on for him on every expense reimbursement save a gross-up and an imputed
-- benefit, and on none of clothing, recuperation and the jubilee grant the
-- track pays its retirees. ¶2: the rest of that agreement stands.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_3 akn:chp_4__art_4 akn:chp_4__art_7__para_b akn:chp_4__art_7__para_b/p2
DECLARE `where the 2009 pension agreement sends a payment` IS ONE OF
    `the budgetary pension, under 30.12.2009`
    `the accrual fund, under 30.12.2009`
    `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`
    `no contribution, under 30.12.2009`

GIVEN p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A `where the 2009 pension agreement sends a payment`
DECIDE `where a permanent teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a component of the budgetary determining salary, of 2009` THEN `the budgetary pension, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `clothing paid to the budgetary track's retirees, of 2009` THEN `the budgetary pension, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `recuperation pay or the jubilee grant, of 2009` THEN `the budgetary pension, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `an expense reimbursement, of 2009` THEN `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit, of 2009` THEN `no contribution, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `another salary component, of 2009` THEN `the accrual fund, under 30.12.2009`

-- The part of a payment for a position up to 100% (§3 here, §3 of chapter
-- ה'): a payment for a larger position counts in its share of a full one.
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER, `the position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part of a payment up to a full position, under 30.12.2009` `the payment` `the position` IS
    IF `the position` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `the payment` DIVIDED BY `the position`
    ELSE `the payment`

#ASSERT `the part of a payment up to a full position, under 30.12.2009` 1200 1.2 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the part of a payment up to a full position, under 30.12.2009` 600 0.5 EQUALS 600

-- §5: the agreement changes neither the pension base of the budgetary track
-- nor its updating — the "determining salary" and the "permanent addition"
-- of §8 of the Pensions Law, and their recognition after the determining
-- day as the law will be. §6: a component in that base on the signing stays
-- in it and does not become one with accrual contributions. §11 ¶1: if the
-- determining salary later changes, the new one is the determining salary
-- here; a component it newly takes in that had accrual contributions stops
-- having them, and the State may have its share back by the law and the
-- capital-market commissioner's directions.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_5 akn:chp_4__art_6 akn:chp_4__art_11
GIVEN `in the determining salary now` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `where the 2009 pension agreement sends a payment`
DECIDE `where a permanent teacher's other component goes as the determining salary changes` `in the determining salary now` IS
    IF `in the determining salary now`
    THEN `where a permanent teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` `a component of the budgetary determining salary, of 2009`
    ELSE `where a permanent teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` `another salary component, of 2009`

#ASSERT `where a permanent teacher's other component goes as the determining salary changes` TRUE EQUALS `the budgetary pension, under 30.12.2009`

`the State may have its share back on a component the determining salary takes in` MEANS TRUE

-- §11 ¶2: if a permanent teacher, retired, is in fact paid a budgetary
-- pension on a component that had accrual contributions for the same
-- period, the parties discuss how the employer's share is returned. ¶3:
-- chapter י"ג's committee decides disputes over this section.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_11/p2 akn:chp_4__art_11/p3
GIVEN `paid a budgetary pension on a component that had accrual contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2009 teachers' pension action`
DECIDE `discussing the State's share on a doubly-covered component` `paid a budgetary pension on a component that had accrual contributions` IS
    IF `paid a budgetary pension on a component that had accrual contributions`
    THEN PARTY `the State`
         MUST  `discuss returning the State's share on a component the budgetary pension pays`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- §7(א): §3's accrual contributions come, for the permanent teacher, in
-- place of the agreement of 17.12.98 (הסכם הגמל) on the components §3
-- covers, from when §3's contributions start. §8: §§3 and 7 come in place of
-- §9 of that agreement (its move to pension contributions, here made). §9:
-- §3 comes in place of what the reform agreements of 10.9.07 and 25.12.08
-- say on provident-fund contributions on those components, from the same
-- day. §10: never twice on one component for one period, under this
-- agreement, הסכם הגמל, the agreement of 27.12.84 or the reform agreements.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_7 akn:chp_4__art_7__para_a akn:chp_4__art_8 akn:chp_4__art_9 akn:chp_4__art_10
GIVEN d IS A DATE, p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 17.12.98 still contributes on a permanent teacher's payment on` d p IF
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2009)
    THEN `where a permanent teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` p EQUALS `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`
    ELSE `the 1998 Histadrut provident-fund agreement contributes on` d (`the 1998 payment for` p) (`the 1998 pension for` p)

GIVEN p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A `payment the 1998 provident-fund agreement tells apart`
DECIDE `the 1998 payment for` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a component of the budgetary determining salary, of 2009` THEN `a pensionable payment`
    WHEN `clothing paid to the budgetary track's retirees, of 2009` THEN `the clothing allowance payment`
    WHEN `recuperation pay or the jubilee grant, of 2009` THEN `the jubilee grant`
    WHEN `an expense reimbursement, of 2009` THEN `an expense reimbursement payment`
    WHEN `a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit, of 2009` THEN `a tax gross-up payment`
    WHEN `another salary component, of 2009` THEN `another payment that is not pensionable`

GIVEN p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A `pension of the 1998 provident-fund agreement's teacher`
DECIDE `the 1998 pension for` p IS `a budgetary pension`

#ASSERT `the 1998 Histadrut provident-fund agreement contributes on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2008) `another payment that is not pensionable` `a budgetary pension`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 17.12.98 still contributes on a permanent teacher's payment on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2009) `another salary component, of 2009`
#ASSERT `the agreement of 17.12.98 still contributes on a permanent teacher's payment on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2009) `an expense reimbursement, of 2009`

GIVEN `contributions under the other agreements for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2009 pension agreement contributes on a component already covered` `contributions under the other agreements for the period` IF
    NOT `contributions under the other agreements for the period`

§§ `פרק ה' — עובד הוראה קיים ועובד הוראה חדש`

-- akn:chp_5 The heading of chapter ה'.

-- §1: the existing teaching employees stay insured in an accrual fund,
-- from 1.1.09 on §3's base. §2: the new ones are insured in one.
@ref akn:chp_5__art_1 akn:chp_5__art_2
GIVEN s IS A `2009 teaching employee's status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `insured in an accrual fund under 30.12.2009` s IF
    s EQUALS `existing, under the 2009 pension agreement` OR s EQUALS `new, under the 2009 pension agreement`

-- §3: from 1.1.09 the monthly base for the accrual fund of an existing or
-- new teacher is (א) and (ב) together: (א) every component in a permanent
-- teacher's determining salary for the budgetary pension, for a position
-- up to 100%, save clothing and with the jubilee grant and recuperation;
-- (ב) every other component up to 100% that is not an expense
-- reimbursement, a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit, and save clothing.
-- §4: by the law that applies. §5(ב): the provident-fund contribution of
-- הסכם הגמל goes on, or is made, on every expense reimbursement save a
-- gross-up and an imputed benefit, and on clothing; ¶2: the rest of that
-- agreement stands.
@ref akn:chp_5__art_3 akn:chp_5__art_3__para_a akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b akn:chp_5__art_4 akn:chp_5__art_5__para_b akn:chp_5__art_5__para_b/p2
GIVEN p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A `where the 2009 pension agreement sends a payment`
DECIDE `where an existing or new teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a component of the budgetary determining salary, of 2009` THEN `the accrual fund, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `clothing paid to the budgetary track's retirees, of 2009` THEN `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `recuperation pay or the jubilee grant, of 2009` THEN `the accrual fund, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `an expense reimbursement, of 2009` THEN `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit, of 2009` THEN `no contribution, under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN `another salary component, of 2009` THEN `the accrual fund, under 30.12.2009`

GIVEN s IS A `2009 teaching employee's status`, p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A `where the 2009 pension agreement sends a payment`
DECIDE `where a payment goes under 30.12.2009` s p IS
    BRANCH IF s EQUALS `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement` THEN `where a permanent teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` p
           IF `insured in an accrual fund under 30.12.2009` s THEN `where an existing or new teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` p
           OTHERWISE `no contribution, under 30.12.2009`

-- the jubilee grant and recuperation: in the budgetary base of a
-- permanent teacher, in the accrual base of an existing or new one
#ASSERT `where a payment goes under 30.12.2009` `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement` `recuperation pay or the jubilee grant, of 2009` EQUALS `the budgetary pension, under 30.12.2009`
#ASSERT `where a payment goes under 30.12.2009` `new, under the 2009 pension agreement` `recuperation pay or the jubilee grant, of 2009` EQUALS `the accrual fund, under 30.12.2009`
#ASSERT `where a payment goes under 30.12.2009` `existing, under the 2009 pension agreement` `clothing paid to the budgetary track's retirees, of 2009` EQUALS `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`

-- §5(א): §3(ב)'s contributions come, for the existing and new teachers,
-- in place of הסכם הגמל on the components §3(ב) covers, from when they
-- start. §6: §3 comes in place of the reform agreements' provident-fund
-- contributions on those components. §7: never twice on one component for
-- one period (as chapter ד' §10).
@ref akn:chp_5__art_5 akn:chp_5__art_5__para_a akn:chp_5__art_6 akn:chp_5__art_7
GIVEN d IS A DATE, p IS A `payment the 2009 pension agreement tells apart`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 17.12.98 still contributes on an existing or new teacher's payment on` d p IF
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2009)
    THEN `where an existing or new teacher's payment goes under 30.12.2009` p EQUALS `the provident fund of 17.12.98, under 30.12.2009`
    ELSE `the 1998 Histadrut provident-fund agreement contributes on` d (`the 1998 payment for` p) (`the 1998 pension for` p)

#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 17.12.98 still contributes on an existing or new teacher's payment on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2009) `another salary component, of 2009`

-- §8: none of this — the contributions of chapter ד' §3 and chapter ה' §3
-- among them — changes what was the practice until the determining day on
-- (א) the budgetary track's determining salary, (ב) the components counted
-- for severance, (ג) the components with study-fund contributions, (ד) the
-- hour value.
-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §8(ב) changes nothing in
-- the components counted for severance; which components count, §13 of
-- the law sends to the regulations, and this rules nothing there.
@ref akn:chp_5__art_8 akn:chp_5__art_8__para_a akn:chp_5__art_8__para_b akn:chp_5__art_8__para_c akn:chp_5__art_8__para_d
DECLARE `what §8 of chapter ה' keeps as it was` IS ONE OF
    `the budgetary track's determining salary, as §8 keeps it`
    `the components counted for severance, as §8 keeps them`
    `the components with study-fund contributions, as §8 keeps them`
    `the hour value, as §8 keeps it`

GIVEN k IS A `what §8 of chapter ה' keeps as it was`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2009 contributions change` k IF FALSE

§§ `פרק ו' — ההפרשות לקופת גמל לקצבה`

-- akn:chp_6 The heading of chapter ו'.

-- §1: from 1.1.09 the State contributes monthly to the accrual fund (א)
-- for a permanent teacher 13.5% (7.5% of it for benefits) of the insured
-- salary of chapter ד' §3; (ב) for an existing or new one 13.724% (7.5% for
-- benefits) of the insured salary of chapter ה' §3. ¶2: on account of
-- benefits and in place of severance, as chapter ז' says, and subject to
-- (ג).
@ref akn:chp_6__art_1 akn:chp_6__art_1__para_a akn:chp_6__art_1__para_b akn:chp_6__art_1/p2
GIVEN s IS A `2009 teaching employee's status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the State's accrual contribution rate under 30.12.2009` s IS
    BRANCH IF s EQUALS `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement` THEN 13.5%
           IF `insured in an accrual fund under 30.12.2009` s THEN 13.724%
           OTHERWISE 0

`the benefits part of the State's contribution under 30.12.2009` MEANS 7.5%

-- For the permanent teacher the rest, 6%, is 72% of a month's wage a year
-- (8⅓%), the share chapter ז' names for the existing and new ones. The
-- 13.724% is not split further by the agreement.
#ASSERT `the State's accrual contribution rate under 30.12.2009` `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement` MINUS `the benefits part of the State's contribution under 30.12.2009` EQUALS 72% DIVIDED BY 12

-- (ג): on the personal supplement the reform agreements pay a principal
-- or a first deputy principal, 8⅓% comes in place of the whole of
-- severance, and the rest of (א) or (ב)'s rate goes to benefits.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_1__para_c
`the severance part on a principal's personal supplement under 30.12.2009` MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY 12

GIVEN s IS A `2009 teaching employee's status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the benefits part on a principal's personal supplement under 30.12.2009` s IS
    `the State's accrual contribution rate under 30.12.2009` s MINUS `the severance part on a principal's personal supplement under 30.12.2009`

-- §2: what the State contributed for 1.1.09–31.12.09 — 5% for the
-- permanent teachers (by הסכם הגמל or the reform agreements), 12% (as a
-- "new employee" of the Pensions Law) or 5% for the existing and new ones —
-- is on account of §1's contributions, and none is made twice.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_2
GIVEN `contributed for the month in 2009` IS A NUMBER, `owed under §1 for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2009 contribution still owed for a month of 2009` `contributed for the month in 2009` `owed under §1 for the month` IS
    max 0 (`owed under §1 for the month` MINUS `contributed for the month in 2009`)

#ASSERT `the employer's provident-fund contribution under the 1998 Histadrut agreement` EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the 2009 contribution still owed for a month of 2009` (5% TIMES 1000) (13.5% TIMES 1000) EQUALS 85

-- §3: the State deducts 5.5% of the insured salary each month and passes
-- it to the fund; on a teacher's written request it lowers his part to the
-- least the law sets (5% on the signing) or raises it beyond 5.5%, up to
-- the ceiling the law sets (7% on the signing). Both bounds are the law's
-- and move with it: inputs. "כמשמעותו בס"ק א' דלעיל": F-teachers-pension-2009-b.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_3
`the teacher's deduction under 30.12.2009` MEANS 5.5%

#ASSERT `the teacher's deduction under 30.12.2009` EQUALS `the employee's accrual deduction under the 1999 agreement`

GIVEN `the rate he asked for in writing` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the least the law sets` IS A NUMBER @desc 5% on the signing
      `the ceiling the law sets` IS A NUMBER @desc 7% on the signing
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the teacher's deduction rate under 30.12.2009` `the rate he asked for in writing` `the least the law sets` `the ceiling the law sets` IS
    CONSIDER `the rate he asked for in writing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the teacher's deduction under 30.12.2009`
    WHEN JUST r THEN min `the ceiling the law sets` (max `the least the law sets` r)

#ASSERT `the teacher's deduction rate under 30.12.2009` NOTHING (5%) (7%) EQUALS 5.5%
#ASSERT `the teacher's deduction rate under 30.12.2009` (JUST (4%)) (5%) (7%) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the teacher's deduction rate under 30.12.2009` (JUST (8%)) (5%) (7%) EQUALS 7%

-- F-teachers-pension-2009-b: §3 measures the deduction on "the insured
-- salary, as meant in sub-section א' above", and §3 has no sub-section; the
-- insured salary is §1's, (א) for a permanent teacher and (ב) for an
-- existing or new one (convention reading.misprint).
`the sub-sections §3 of chapter ו' has` MEANS 0
`§3 of chapter ו' cites a sub-section א' it does not have` MEANS
    `the sub-sections §3 of chapter ו' has` LESS THAN 1
#ASSERT `§3 of chapter ו' cites a sub-section א' it does not have`

-- Against the Wage Protection Law (MMS-601): §3's deduction is a current
-- payment to a provident fund, which §25(א)(5) of the law permits; §1's
-- contribution and §3's deduction are passed each month with the month's
-- wage, within the 21 days §19א(א) gives after the determining day.
#ASSERT `section 25 of the Wage Protection Law permits the deduction` `a current provident-fund payment (5) allows`
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument's day for a contribution is later than section 19א allows` (`the day a monthly wage falls due under section 9` 30) (`the day a monthly wage falls due under section 9` 30)

-- §4: notwithstanding §3, for 1.1.09–31.12.09 the deduction made — 5% by
-- הסכם הגמל or the reform agreements, or 5.5% by the Pensions Law — comes
-- in place of §3's, and nothing more is deducted for that period.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_4
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `deducted in 2009` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2009 deduction still owed for` d `deducted in 2009` IS
    IF d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2009) THEN 0
    ELSE `the teacher's deduction under 30.12.2009`

-- §5: nothing here takes from the Supervision of Financial Services
-- (Insurance) Law, 1981, or any law on the rates of payment to an accrual
-- fund; this agreement applies beside them.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_5
`the 2009 pension agreement takes from the law on fund rates` MEANS FALSE

§§ `פרק ז' — השלמה לפיצויי פיטורים`

-- akn:chp_7 The heading of chapter ז'.

-- §1: for an existing or new teacher the State's payments to the fund in
-- respect of severance come in place of the whole 72% of severance under
-- §14 of the Severance Pay Law, on the components counted for severance
-- (by this agreement or as they will be), up to a full position, that
-- carried contributions, for the period they did. §2: the State pays him
-- the rest, 28% of those components of his last salary, up to a full
-- position, times his years with the employer and his weighted position
-- share (up to 100%), at an event entitling to severance or at the end of
-- work with a pension from the fund (age, disability or survivors) — and
-- to a teacher or survivors with no pension from the fund, for want of the
-- minimum or for a disability or survivors' pension under a law. ¶2: tax
-- on it is the teacher's; the State pays no gross-up.
@ref akn:chp_7__art_1 akn:chp_7__art_2 akn:chp_7__art_2/p2
`the share of severance the 2009 contributions take the place of` MEANS 72%
`the share of severance the State pays at the end, under 30.12.2009` MEANS 28%

#ASSERT `the share of severance the 2009 contributions take the place of` PLUS `the share of severance the State pays at the end, under 30.12.2009` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the share of severance the 2009 contributions take the place of` EQUALS `the share of severance the contributions take the place of`

GIVEN s IS A `2009 teaching employee's status`
      `the last salary's components that carried contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `years with the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the weighted position share` IS A NUMBER
      `an entitling event, or the end of work with or without a pension from the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance completion under 30.12.2009` s `the last salary's components that carried contributions` `years with the employer` `the weighted position share` `an entitling event, or the end of work with or without a pension from the fund` IS
    IF     `insured in an accrual fund under 30.12.2009` s
       AND `an entitling event, or the end of work with or without a pension from the fund`
    THEN `the share of severance the State pays at the end, under 30.12.2009`
             TIMES `the last salary's components that carried contributions`
             TIMES `years with the employer`
             TIMES min 1 `the weighted position share`
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the severance completion under 30.12.2009` `new, under the 2009 pension agreement` 10000 10 1 TRUE EQUALS 28000
#ASSERT `the severance completion under 30.12.2009` `new, under the 2009 pension agreement` 10000 10 0.5 TRUE EQUALS 14000
#ASSERT `the severance completion under 30.12.2009` `permanent, under the 2009 pension agreement` 10000 10 1 TRUE EQUALS 0

-- Against the Severance Pay Law (l4/laws/severance-pay-law.l4): §14 lets
-- the contributions take the place of severance as far as the collective
-- agreement says, 72%, and the employer owes the rest of §12's month for
-- each year; chapter ז' pays exactly that. On the principal's personal
-- supplement chapter ו' §1(ג) sets the whole, and the employer owes none.
-- §§4–5 keep the whole of the law's severance on a component or a period
-- with no contribution, or a partial one.
`chapter ז' completes exactly what §14 leaves the State` MEANS
    `the severance completion under 30.12.2009` `new, under the 2009 pension agreement` 10000 10 1 TRUE
        EQUALS `the severance the employer still owes under section 14`
                   (`severance pay under section 12` `salaried, by the month or longer, under section 12` 10000 10)
                   (`the share of severance a fund payment takes the place of under section 14` `the share of severance the 2009 contributions take the place of` 0)
#ASSERT `chapter ז' completes exactly what §14 leaves the State`

#ASSERT `the severance the employer still owes under section 14` 50000 (`the share of severance a fund payment takes the place of under section 14` (`the severance part on a principal's personal supplement under 30.12.2009` TIMES 12) 0) EQUALS 0

-- §3: none of this reaches the principal's supplement of chapter ו' §1(ג).
-- §4: a teacher entitled to severance by law keeps the whole of it on a
-- component with no, or a partial, contribution; §5: and for a period with
-- no contribution on any component. §6: his rights under the agreement of
-- 27.12.84 (Dafna) are kept. §7: none of this for a permanent teacher on
-- the budgetary track: if entitled to severance, the track's rules in the
-- State's service apply.
@ref akn:chp_7__art_3 akn:chp_7__art_4 akn:chp_7__art_5 akn:chp_7__art_6 akn:chp_7__art_7
GIVEN `the law's severance on the component and period` IS A NUMBER
      `the share the contributions covered` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 with no contribution, 72% with a full one
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance the State still owes on a component under 30.12.2009` `the law's severance on the component and period` `the share the contributions covered` IS
    `the severance the employer still owes under section 14` `the law's severance on the component and period`
        (`the share of severance a fund payment takes the place of under section 14` `the share the contributions covered` 0)

#ASSERT `the severance the State still owes on a component under 30.12.2009` 10000 0 EQUALS 10000

`the 2009 pension agreement takes from the Dafna agreement of 27.12.84` MEANS FALSE

§§ `פרק ח' — משיכת כספים על-ידי המעסיק`

-- akn:chp_8 The heading of chapter ח'.

-- §1: the fund returns to the State, and the State may ask for, 6% of the
-- contributions it paid, by the law, where the teacher resigned or was
-- dismissed with no right to severance, left the fund and drew his money;
-- with partial severance only, the share of the 6% the partial severance
-- leaves. Subject to that, at the end of the employment he is entitled to
-- a release letter for all the State's money in the fund. §2: a draw is no
-- draw here when (א) made at an entitling event with less than the fund's
-- minimum for a pension, (ב) by survivors not entitled to a pension, or
-- (ג) by one recognised as disabled who has no, or a reduced, disability
-- pension from the fund. §3: a move between accrual funds the law allows is
-- no draw. The words are the 1999 agreement's chapter ט', and so is the
-- rule (imported).
@ref akn:chp_8__art_1 akn:chp_8__art_2 akn:chp_8__art_2__para_a akn:chp_8__art_2__para_b akn:chp_8__art_2__para_c akn:chp_8__art_3
`the share of the State's contributions that may come back under 30.12.2009` MEANS 6%

#ASSERT `the share of the State's contributions that may come back under 30.12.2009` EQUALS `the share of the employer's contributions that may come back`

GIVEN `the share of severance he was entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 with no right to severance, 1 with full
      `left the fund and drew his money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draw is one §§2–3 except` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate that comes back to the State under 30.12.2009` `the share of severance he was entitled to` `left the fund and drew his money` `the draw is one §§2–3 except` IS
    `the rate that comes back to the employer` `the share of severance he was entitled to`
        (`left the fund and drew his money` AND NOT `the draw is one §§2–3 except`)

#ASSERT `the rate that comes back to the State under 30.12.2009` 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 6%
#ASSERT `the rate that comes back to the State under 30.12.2009` 0.5 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `the rate that comes back to the State under 30.12.2009` 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `פרק ט' — בחירת קופת גמל לקצבה`

-- akn:chp_9 The heading of chapter ט'.

-- §1: הסתדרות המורים tells the State the fund or funds it chose. §2: a
-- teacher is insured in the fund he chose. §3: one who does not tell the
-- State in writing, within two months of the signing or of starting work,
-- whichever is later, of the fund he chose — (א) an existing or new one
-- insured in a fund for (א)'s components on the signing is insured in it
-- for (ב)'s too; (ב) a permanent one, and a new one not insured in a fund
-- in the State's service on the signing, in the union's fund — until he
-- tells of another. §4: for 1.1.09–31.12.09, (א) and (ב) apply whatever
-- the opening of §3 says. §5: his right by law to move between funds, or
-- to change the fund the contributions go to, is kept.
@ref akn:chp_9__art_1 akn:chp_9__art_2 akn:chp_9__art_3 akn:chp_9__art_3__para_a akn:chp_9__art_3__para_b akn:chp_9__art_4 akn:chp_9__art_5
`telling the State of the union's funds` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    MUST  `notify the State of the funds the union chose`

GIVEN `the union's fund` IS A STRING
      `the fund he is insured in for (א)'s components` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the fund he told the State of in time` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the fund a teacher is insured in by chapter ט'` `the union's fund` `the fund he is insured in for (א)'s components` `the fund he told the State of in time` IS
    `the fund an employee is insured in by chapter י'` `the union's fund` `the fund he is insured in for (א)'s components` `the fund he told the State of in time`

#ASSERT `the fund a teacher is insured in by chapter ט'` "א" NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS "א"
#ASSERT `the fund a teacher is insured in by chapter ט'` "א" (JUST "ב") NOTHING EQUALS "ב"

`the days a teacher has to tell the State of his fund, as months` MEANS 2

§§ `פרקים י'–ט"ז`

-- akn:chp_10 akn:chp_11 akn:chp_12 akn:chp_13 akn:chp_14 akn:chp_15 akn:chp_16 The headings of chapters י' to ט"ז.

